    "knowledge_point": "Finding the Reduced Row Echelon Form of a 3x3 System That Is Not in Row Echelon Form",
    "problem": "Consider the following system of linear equations:\n\n$$\n{\\begin{aligned} & x-3y=1 \\\\  & y+2z=1 \\\\  & 5x-7y+17z=7\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nUse the standard Gauss-Jordan method to reduce the augmented matrix $M$ of the system to reduced row echelon form.",
    "worked_solution": "The augmented matrix for this system is\n\n$$\nM=[\\begin{aligned}1 & -3 & 0 & 1 \\\\ 0 & 1 & 2 & 1 \\\\ 5 & -7 & 17 & 7\\end{aligned}].\n$$\n\nTransforming $M$ to reduced row echelon form, we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}M & ∼[\\begin{aligned}1 & -3 & 0 & 1 \\\\ 0 & 1 & 2 & 1 \\\\ 5 & -7 & 17 & 7\\end{aligned}] & {R}_{3} & :={R}_{3}+(-5){R}_{1} \\\\  & ∼[\\begin{aligned}1 & -3 & 0 & 1 \\\\ 0 & 1 & 2 & 1 \\\\ 0 & 8 & 17 & 2\\end{aligned}] & {R}_{3} & :={R}_{3}+(-8){R}_{2} \\\\  & ∼[\\begin{aligned}1 & -3 & 0 & 1 \\\\ 0 & 1 & 2 & 1 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 1 & -6\\end{aligned}] & {R}_{2} & :={R}_{2}+(-2){R}_{3} \\\\  & ∼[\\begin{aligned}1 & -3 & 0 & 1 \\\\ 0 & 1 & 0 & 13 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 1 & -6\\end{aligned}] & {R}_{1} & :={R}_{1}+3{R}_{2} \\\\  & ∼[\\begin{aligned}1 & 0 & 0 & 40 \\\\ 0 & 1 & 0 & 13 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 1 & -6\\end{aligned}].\\end{aligned}\n$$",
